{"step_index":1078,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:43:48Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:43:48+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:43:48+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///tmp/agyhome.NWyWnj/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/0d77a839-cb15-4b7b-9247-e4cbcb2ae788/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl`\nTotal Lines: 249\nTotal Bytes: 302972\nShowing lines 1 to 249\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: 77a839-cb15-4b7b-9247-e4cbcb2ae788/task-230 priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=Task id \\\"0d77a839-cb15-4b7b-9247-e4cbcb2ae788/task-230\\\" finished with result:\\n\\nThe command exited with code 0.\\nOutput:\\nLINT: ok\\r\\n'radius_le_eccentricity' depends on axioms: [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]\\r\\nCHECK: elaborated. Allowed axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound.\\r\\n       'sorryAx' in a list above means that theorem is unfinished.\\r\\n\\n\\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\"}\n2: {\"step_index\":237,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T18:42:44Z\",\"thinking\":\"**Deducing graph properties using walks**\\n\\nVerified two key results. Examining what can be further deduced using walk properties.  If every vertex has a walk of length less than or equal to k to the center vertex v, then the ball around v of radius k is the entire vertex set. Consequently, the eccentricity of v is less than or equal to k (given k is no larger than the graph's cardinality), and radius is less than or equal to eccentricity.\\n\\n\\n**Examining the implications of roman domination**\\n\\nConsidering the case where the roman weight is less than the graph's cardinality, a vertex of value 0 must exist. The Roman dominating function ensures a vertex of value 2 also exists. Every vertex with a value 0 must have a value 2 neighbor. If the vertex with value 2 is adjacent to *every* vertex of value 0, then a walk of length 1 exists between the value 2 vertex and every value 0 vertex.\\n\\n\\n**Bounding graph radius using walk properties**\\n\\nA walk of length zero exists from the center vertex `c` to itself. Analyzing walks from `c` to vertices within a specific set, using the connected property to deduce the walk length.  A direct path from `c` to any vertex in `V_0` requires only one step. If the first step goes to another vertex in `V_1`, then the path length to `w` is at most $1+|V_1|$ steps.\\n\\nThe roman weight relationship implies $1 + |V_1|$ equals roman weight minus one. This implies that the radius of the graph is less than or equal to the roman weight minus one. This can also be interpreted as the radius of graph + 1 is less than or equal to romanWeight of f.\\n\\nFurther, the ball around `c` of radius $|V_1|$ covers the entire graph, making the eccentricity of `c` equal to at most the roman weight minus 1. This strengthens the previous conclusion about the graph radius.\\n\\n\\n**Refining bounds using graph properties**\\n\\nThe initial deduction that `radius G + 1 ≤ romanWeight f` seems sound. The lemma `card_ballWithin_succ_of_ne_univ` is important. This, along with `card_ballWithin_add`, leads to the conclusion that if the graph's cardinality is less than or equal to `(ballWithin G k v).card + m`, then `ballWithin G (k + m) v = univ`.\\n\\nThis logic will now be tested by integrating lemmas in the existing code. Adding `card_ballWithin_add` and `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_card_add` to `scratch.lean` is necessary for further analysis, the proof will be by induction.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"replace_file_content\",\"args\":{\"AllowMultiple\":\"false\",\"Description\":\"\\\"Add card_ballWithin_add and ballWithin_eq_univ_of_card_add\\\"\",\"EndLine\":\"257\",\"Instruction\":\"\\\"Append card_ballWithin_add and ballWithin_eq_univ_of_card_add\\\"\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"\\\"lemma ballWithin_eq_univ_of_forall_walk {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) (k : ℕ)\\\\n    (h : ∀ w : V, ∃ p : G.Walk v w, p.length ≤ k) :\\\\n    ballWithin G k v = Finset.univ := by\\\\n  ext w\\\\n  simp only [Finset.mem_univ, iff_true]\\\\n  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := h w\\\\n  exact mem_ballWithin_of_walk_le G p hp\\\\n\\\\nlemma card_ballWithin_add {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V)\\\\n    (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G) (k m : ℕ) :\\\\n    ballWithin G (k + m) v = Finset.univ ∨ (ballWithin G k v).card + m ≤ (ballWithin G (k + m) v).card := by\\\\n  induction m with\\\\n  | zero => right; omega\\\\n  | succ m ih =>\\\\n    cases ih with\\\\n    | inl h_univ =>\\\\n      left\\\\n      have hsub := ballWithin_subset_succ G (k + m) v\\\\n      rw [h_univ] at hsub\\\\n      ext x\\\\n      exact ⟨fun _ => Finset.mem_univ x, fun _ => hsub (Finset.mem_univ x)⟩\\\\n    | inr h_card =>\\\\n      by_cases hne : ballWithin G (k + m) v = Finset.univ\\\\n      · left\\\\n        have hsub := ballWithin_subset_succ G (k + m) v\\\\n        rw [hne] at hsub\\\\n        ext x\\\\n        exact ⟨fun _ => Finset.mem_univ x, fun _ => hsub (Finset.mem_univ x)⟩\\\\n      · right\\\\n        have hstep := card_ballWithin_succ_of_ne_univ G (k + m) v hrad hne\\\\n        omega\\\\n\\\\nlemma ballWithin_eq_univ_of_card_add {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V)\\\\n    (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G) (k m : ℕ)\\\\n    (h : Fintype.card V ≤ (ballWithin G k v).card + m) :\\\\n    ballWithin G (k + m) v = Finset.univ := by\\\\n  have h_cases := card_ballWithin_add G v hrad k m\\\\n  cases h_cases with\\\\n  | inl h_univ => exact h_univ\\\\n  | inr h_card =>\\\\n    by_contra hc\\\\n    have h_ssub : ballWithin G (k + m) v ⊂ Finset.univ := Finset.ssubset_univ_iff.mpr hc\\\\n    have h_lt := Finset.card_lt_card h_ssub\\\\n    rw [Finset.card_univ] at h_lt\\\\n    omega\\\\n\\\"\",\"StartLine\":\"244\",\"TargetContent\":\"\\\"lemma ballWithin_eq_univ_of_forall_walk {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) (k : ℕ)\\\\n    (h : ∀ w : V, ∃ p : G.Walk v w, p.length ≤ k) :\\\\n    ballWithin G k v = Finset.univ := by\\\\n  ext w\\\\n  simp only [Finset.mem_univ, iff_true]\\\\n  obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := h w\\\\n  exact mem_ballWithin_of_walk_le G p hp\\\"\",\"TargetFile\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/scratch.lean\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Adding card_ballWithin_add to scratch.lean\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"Add card_ballWithin_add\\\"\"}}]}\n3: {\"step_index\":238,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T18:43:05Z\",\"content\":\"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:43:05+02:00\\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:43:08+02:00\\nThe following changes were made by the replace_file_content tool to: /mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/scratch.lean. If relevant, proactively run terminal commands to execute this code for the USER. Don't ask for permission.\\n[diff_block_start]\\n@@ -254,6 +254,47 @@\\n   obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := h w\\n   exact mem_ballWithin_of_walk_le G p hp\\n \\n+lemma card_ballWithin_add {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n+    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V)\\n+    (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G) (k m : ℕ) :\\n+    ballWithin G (k + m) v = Finset.univ ∨ (ballWithin G k v).card + m ≤ (ballWithin G (k + m) v).card := by\\n+  induction m with\\n+  | zero => right; omega\\n+  | succ m ih =>\\n+    cases ih with\\n+    | inl h_univ =>\\n+      left\\n+      have hsub := ballWithin_subset_succ G (k + m) v\\n+      rw [h_univ] at hsub\\n+      ext x\\n+      exact ⟨fun _ => Finset.mem_univ x, fun _ => hsub (Finset.mem_univ x)⟩\\n+    